# general syllabic contractions

# The contractions on and ion have no position restrictions (they may follow a vowel or start
# a word), but they are not used when the vowel is accented (león, iónico: those letters
# are different characters here) nor for the whole word ion.

attribute consonants BbCcDdFfGgHhJjKkLlMmNnPpQqRrSsTtVvWwXxYyZzÑñ
always on 1346
always ion 3456
# The u e contraction may never be used after the letter g, avoids confussion with u
# diaeresis which is part of many words (B 16-1 v3, 3.4.2 rule 3: sigue, not sig + ue).
attribute euvowels Gg
after euvowels always eu 15-136
after euvowels always EU 15-136
after euvowels always ue 136-15
after euvowels always UE 136-15
after euvowels endword ue 136-15

# only exception to this contraction, avoids confussion with the Spanish comma at end of words

partword ad 1456
partword al 13
partword an 146
partword ar 16
partword as 12346
partword em 126
partword es 1246
partword im 345
partword ion 3456
partword ll 123456
partword om 2456
partword or 156
partword os 246
partword qu 12345
partword ue 1256

# sequences (Documento tecnico B 16-1, version 3, 3.3): groups of letters that are written with the
# sign of a one-cell word. Like principles and endings they have priority over contractions.

# que: at the beginning and in the middle of a word; at the end it is the ending -que
begmidword que 12345
# para: anywhere
partword para 456-16
# ante: at the beginning and in the middle; at the end of a word the ending -te is used,
# after the contraction an
begmidword ante 456-146
endword antes 146-2345-234
endword antemente 146-2345-134
endword anteando 146-2345-146-145
endword antedad 146-2345-1456
endword antedades 146-2345-1456-1246
# para and esta are followed by the ending -ando: the ending has priority, the sequence
# does not use its last letter (parando, gestando)
endword parando 1234-16-146-145
endword parandos 1234-16-146-145-234
word parando 1234-16-146-145
word parandos 1234-16-146-145-234
endword estando 1246-2345-146-145
# esta: before a consonant at the beginning, between consonants in the middle and after a
# consonant at the end
before consonants begword esta 1356
after consonants before consonants midword esta 1356
after consonants endword esta 1356

