# Names of countries made of several words: Costa Rica 456-14-1235, El Salvador 456-234-1236,
# Republica Dominicana 456-145-135. A rule cannot contain a space, so each word is translated on
# its own (with its capital sign) and the second pass replaces the whole expression, space
# included, by the sign of the name. Only when what follows is not a letter, as for the other
# countries. The cells
# are the ones the words have in the first pass (costa = c + os + t + a, salvador = s + al + v +
# ad + or).

noback pass2 [@46@14@246@2345@1@0@46@1235@24@14@1]!$l @456@14@1235
noback pass2 [@46@14@246@2345@1@0@46@1235@24@14@1]~ @456@14@1235
noback pass2 [@46@46@14@246@2345@1@0@46@46@1235@24@14@1]!$l @456@14@1235
noback pass2 [@46@46@14@246@2345@1@0@46@46@1235@24@14@1]~ @456@14@1235
noback pass2 [@46@15@0@46@234@13@1236@1456@156]!$l @456@234@1236
noback pass2 [@46@15@0@46@234@13@1236@1456@156]~ @456@234@1236
noback pass2 [@46@46@15@0@46@46@234@13@1236@1456@156]!$l @456@234@1236
noback pass2 [@46@46@15@0@46@46@234@13@1236@1456@156]~ @456@234@1236
noback pass2 [@46@1235@1234@23456@12@123@24@14@1@0@46@145@2456@35@24@14@146@1]!$l @456@145@135
noback pass2 [@46@1235@1234@23456@12@123@24@14@1@0@46@145@2456@35@24@14@146@1]~ @456@145@135
noback pass2 [@46@46@1235@1234@23456@12@123@24@14@1@0@46@46@145@2456@35@24@14@146@1]!$l @456@145@135
noback pass2 [@46@46@1235@1234@23456@12@123@24@14@1@0@46@46@145@2456@35@24@14@146@1]~ @456@145@135

# Word beginnings (principles) are only used before a consonant (Documento tecnico B 16-1,
# version 3, 3.1). Before a vowel the letters are written with their contractions as usual
# (reactivo, comun). The consonant that follows a principle may be contracted (comprar,
# contrato).

# word beginnings

before consonants begword com 36
before consonants begword con 25
before consonants begword dis 256
before consonants begword entre 356
before consonants begword ex 1346
before consonants begword inter 13456
before consonants begword pre 235
before consonants begword pro 1234
before consonants begword re 1235
before consonants begword sobre 23

# Several word beginnings in a row (3.1.1). The last one must precede a consonant. Chains
# ending in pre- include its vowel (comprension, representar).

before consonants begword repre 1235-235
before consonants begword expre 1346-235
before consonants begword compre 36-235
before consonants begword compro 36-1234
before consonants begword interpre 13456-235
before consonants begword sobrepre 23-235
before consonants begword repro 1235-1234
before consonants begword recon 1235-25
before consonants begword recom 1235-36
before consonants begword redis 1235-256
before consonants begword reex 1235-1346
before consonants begword reinter 1235-13456
before consonants begword reentre 1235-356
before consonants begword expro 1346-1234
before consonants begword exre 1346-1235
before consonants begword excon 1346-25
before consonants begword excom 1346-36
before consonants begword interre 13456-1235
before consonants begword intercon 13456-25
before consonants begword interdis 13456-256
before consonants begword interpro 13456-1234
before consonants begword intercom 13456-36
before consonants begword predis 235-256
before consonants begword precon 235-25
before consonants begword prepro 235-1234
before consonants begword preex 235-1346
before consonants begword precom 235-36
before consonants begword discon 256-25
before consonants begword condis 25-256
before consonants begword sobreex 23-1346
before consonants begword sobrepro 23-1234
before consonants begword sobrecom 23-36
before consonants begword sobrecon 23-25
before consonants begword sobreinter 23-13456
before consonants begword sobredis 23-256
before consonants begword sobreentre 23-356
before consonants begword procom 1234-36
before consonants begword procon 1234-25
before consonants begword proex 1234-1346

before consonants begword reinterpre 1235-13456-235
before consonants begword sobreinterpre 23-13456-235
before consonants begword recompre 1235-36-235
before consonants begword sobreexpre 23-1346-235
before consonants begword recompro 1235-36-1234
before consonants begword reexpro 1235-1346-1234
before consonants begword reprepro 1235-235-1234

# A word beginning should be followed by at least a consonant and a vowel or a consonant
# and a stenographic contraction. Some words are thus entirely uncontracted. Again, very
# few ones in the language.

word red 1235-15-145
word rey 1235-15-13456
word res 1235-15-234
word sobren 234-135-23-26
word entren 26-356-26
word sobres 23-1246

# exceptions to the entire table, words which may never be contracted or brailled
# differently to avoid confussion with other contracted words
word vodca 1236-135-14-145-1
word entrenen 26-356-26-26
word as 1-234
word os 135-234
word ion 24-135-1345

# B 16-1 v3, 3.4.2 rule 4: dr is not contracted in the abbreviation Dr. (Dra., Dres., Dras.)
# when the text already has it abbreviated.
match (^|!%a) dr ([.]|a[.]|es[.]|as[.]) 145-1235

# Whenever some partword contractions overlap, such as ad and dr, in a single word
# (ladrillo) the dr contraction is preferred (B 16-1 v3, 3.4.1, Table 19). Setting the seven
# cases where this can occur.

always abr 1-23
always adr 1-256
always all 1-123456
always uen 136-26
always uem 136-126
always uer 136-236
always ues 136-1246

# some cases for word endings (prioritization)

endword emando 126-146-145
endword emandos 126-146-145-234
endword imando 345-146-145
endword imandos 345-146-145-234
